// ── H1/H2 scope hooks ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// MERGE this into .claude/settings.json — do not paste the file wholesale.
// Your settings.json already carries permissions and other hooks; add only the
// entries under the "hooks" key, beside whatever is there.
//
// Why hooks rather than instructions: a boundary an agent is ASKED to respect
// is advisory, and advisory boundaries are the ones that get crossed at 2am
// under deadline. H1 blocks the write; H2 records the one it does not block.
// Both are inert unless a task packet is armed (spec/packets/.active), so they
// cost nothing during work that is not packet-scoped.
//
// H1 (PreToolUse) refuses a write inside the active packet's `must_not_touch`
// globs and names the RU that imposed the boundary. Exit 2 blocks the call.
// H2 (PostToolUse) appends writes outside the packet's `owns` globs to
// spec/projections/scope-audit.jsonl. It never blocks: out-of-owns work is
// accepted residual risk, and the audit trail is what makes it reviewable.

{
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Edit|Write",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/h1-scope-guard.sh\"",
            "timeout": 15
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Edit|Write",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/h2-scope-audit.sh\"",
            "timeout": 15
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}

// NOTE: both scripts read the edited path from the hook's stdin JSON with `jq`,
// and the PostToolUse/PreToolUse payload shape can vary by Claude Code version.
// If a hook goes quiet, verify the payload against code.claude.com/docs →
// Configure settings → hooks for your installed version. The scripts fail open
// by design: a missing `jq`, a missing `rqunit`, or no armed packet all exit 0
// rather than bricking every edit in the repository.
